\title{scholararcs: Citation Arcs for Any Researcher}
\description{
Draws three views of a researcher's citation record: cumulative citations in calendar time, cumulative citations aligned on each paper's publication year, and the per-year arc that shows when papers actually peaked. Papers are coloured by the kind of venue that published them, tiered automatically within the author's own field and overridable by hand. Reads from OpenAlex by default, which works anywhere; a Google Scholar backend is available when the app is run locally.
